  "title": "Noise Complaint",
  "summary": "The body corporate tells Ruth someone has complained about her piano before 8 am. She texts the new man downstairs with ferocious politeness. Iain says he has never complained about anything in his life; he just works nights. They agree a truce, and the texts thaw into song titles and a note about Chopin. Then Ruth asks the body corporate for the complaint record, 'for her files'.",
